            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The article is devoted to modern views of the pathogenesis of postherpetic neuralgia, the risks of its occurrence in patients with herpetic ganglionitis and treatment in the acute period to prevent the development of chronic pain, as well as in the treatment of already developed postherpetic neuralgia with the use of glutamate receptors antagonists.</AbstractText>
